gosh seam 23: what the cipher opens is carried by a type that says how many bytes it may be (Session::Length).

For:   REQ22/SHAPE-1 (since v22, the seam may carry by a type a bound its callers already keep, where
       a proof needs it). Session::decrypt does its arithmetic in int: `int body_len = len - 8;
       int pt_len = body_len - 16;`. Of a length of 2^31 bytes or more, the subtraction may overflow,
       which C++ leaves undefined; what keeps it from that is only that its callers hand it no more
       than they receive, RECEIVE_MTU (2048) bytes. So decrypt cannot be proved free of undefined
       behaviour for every length it may be handed, only for those its callers keep to: the type
       says so, and the proof of decrypt has it (queue item 43 of strong-domain-driven-design).
What:  decrypt( const char* str, size_t len ) takes its length as a Session::Length, a
       Strong::bounded<0, RECEIVE_MTU, size_t> (gosh's src/strong/bounded.h): a number from 0 to
       2048 by its type, which nothing tests. It reads it by len.number(), and nothing else in it
       changes: a datagram shorter than 24 bytes still throws, as it must, since anyone may send
       one. Code that is not proved hands it any number by decrypt_checked( str, len ), which tests
       it (bounded_checked) and ends the process past 2048, saying who called; the network, and the
       std::string overload (so the tests and the example decrypt), call it. Of the network nothing
       changes: it receives into 2048 bytes, so the test never fails. Of the std::string overload,
       a ciphertext past 2048 bytes ended the process before by decrypt's assert, and does now by
       the test, with another message. No byte of the protocol changes, and what a stock mosh sees
       is the same.
Where: src/crypto/crypto.h (Session); src/crypto/imp/crypto.cc (Session::decrypt);
       src/network/imp/network.cc (the one call).
Kind:  a parameter's type changed to one that carries its bound, and a way in for code that is not
       proved added, in the cipher's ABI; seam/DOMAINS allows the cipher's header to include
       src/strong/bounded.h, gosh's, the one crossing from the core into gosh.
From:  the core at the pin: src/crypto/crypto.h, src/crypto/crypto.cc (moved under imp/ by patch 12),
       src/network/network.cc (moved under imp/ by patch 14).
Pin:   upstream mosh at decd9b705eb81626f694335b8d5940538beb06da; cut against the result of the patch before it.

diff --git a/src/crypto/crypto.h b/src/crypto/crypto.h
--- a/src/crypto/crypto.h
+++ b/src/crypto/crypto.h
@@ -34,6 +34,7 @@
 #define CRYPTO_HPP
 
 #include "src/crypto/imp/ae.h"
+#include "src/strong/bounded.h"
 
 #include <cstdint>
 #include <cstdlib>
@@ -156,8 +157,18 @@
   ~Session();
 
   const std::string encrypt( const Message& plaintext );
-  const Message decrypt( const char* str, size_t len );
-  const Message decrypt( const std::string& ciphertext ) { return decrypt( ciphertext.data(), ciphertext.size() ); }
+  /* The number of bytes a sealed datagram may be: no more than is received (gosh seam 23). */
+  typedef Strong::bounded<0, RECEIVE_MTU, size_t> Length;
+
+  /* Opens what was sealed: len bytes at str, of which the type says there are at most RECEIVE_MTU. */
+  const Message decrypt( const char* str, Length len );
+  /* The same, of any number of bytes, for code that is not proved: past RECEIVE_MTU the process
+     ends, saying who called (bounded_checked), where an assert in decrypt ended it before. */
+  const Message decrypt_checked( const char* str, size_t len )
+  {
+    return decrypt( str, Length( Strong::bounded_checked<0, RECEIVE_MTU, size_t>( len ).number() ) );
+  }
+  const Message decrypt( const std::string& ciphertext ) { return decrypt_checked( ciphertext.data(), ciphertext.size() ); }
 
   Session( const Session& );
   Session& operator=( const Session& );
